WEBVTT

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:28.650
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:28.650
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:28.650
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:01:54.230 --> 00:02:02.650
The Retriever
Chapter I

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:27.860
Dead due to a cranial fracture.

00:02:29.050 --> 00:02:29.810
Go !

00:02:29.810 --> 00:02:30.940
Take over the bridge !

00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:39.510
The enemy unit has gotten
past the fifth defense line.

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:40.820
They are about to
enter the upper sector.

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:44.150
Bridge crew, prepare 
for close combat !

00:02:44.150 --> 00:02:45.210
Do not permit their entry !

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:48.750
Hurry !

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:49.500
Don't dawdle !

00:02:50.950 --> 00:02:51.850
Let's go.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:53.500
Hurry up, this way !

00:02:57.930 --> 00:03:00.200
First Officer, take command
of the interception effort.

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:00.750
Yes, sir !

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:05.490
Chief Navigator, continue 
concentrating on your navigation.

00:03:05.490 --> 00:03:07.950
Chief Gunner, Chief Missileer{Torpedo Man},
put on your armored suits.

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:10.850
Captain, please wear 
your armor, too.

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:26.800
Dead due to severed neck.

00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:35.260
Incapacitated due to
severed upper arm.

00:03:54.650 --> 00:03:56.950
Dead due to severed spine.

00:03:56.950 --> 00:04:01.200
Incapacitated due to lacerations
of the chest area that reach the lungs.

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:03.400
Death within thirty minutes.

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:06.650
Incapacitated due to a
fracture of the left leg.

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:16.090
They've broken through
the last defense line.

00:04:16.090 --> 00:04:17.340
The enemy unit will 
reach this area shortly.

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:18.870
Pathetic.

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:20.080
We'll defend this area !

00:04:20.080 --> 00:04:21.110
Fortify the entrance !

00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:26.310
The density of Seffle Particles is rising.

00:04:26.310 --> 00:04:27.520
Firearms cannot be used.

00:04:47.390 --> 00:04:49.050
You're good, Lieutenant Junior Grade !

00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:49.950
You too, sir !

00:05:01.950 --> 00:05:06.390
Normally, it would be a defeat once we 
allow the enemy entrance to the bridge.

00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:23.920
Captain, you'll have to excuse us.

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:34.750
Judgment - dead due to an injury
from the trachea to the hind brain.

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:40.150
I won't have mercy on those
who let their guard down.

00:05:41.150 --> 00:05:42.870
Attack me with the intent to kill !

00:05:45.350 --> 00:05:46.590
You swine !

00:05:54.550 --> 00:05:55.250
Lord Reinhard.

00:05:55.850 --> 00:05:57.000
You let your guard down !

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:57.850
Dammit !

00:06:01.150 --> 00:06:04.930
Judgment - combat capability decreased due to an injury to the right forearm.

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:07.910
Captain !

00:06:17.990 --> 00:06:21.750
It's not just LTJG Kircheis;
our Captain is also good.

00:06:21.750 --> 00:06:24.990
But still, he really is merciless.

00:06:26.250 --> 00:06:29.330
Assault unit annihilated.
Battle exercise complete.

00:06:32.650 --> 00:06:34.530
Good job, No. 1.

00:06:34.530 --> 00:06:35.580
Yes, sir.

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:37.360
Prioritize treatment of the injured.

00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:39.050
Evaluations will be done afterwards.

00:06:39.050 --> 00:06:40.210
Order acknowledged.

00:06:43.230 --> 00:06:46.590
Medical department, confirm and treat the injured immediately.

00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:49.060
And come to the bridge as well.

00:06:49.060 --> 00:06:51.900
Each unit chief, report the
damage in your assigned area.

00:06:51.900 --> 00:06:53.350
Afterwards, we'll withdraw.

00:06:53.350 --> 00:06:53.990
Hurry up.

00:06:56.190 --> 00:06:58.050
It was a complete defeat on my part.

00:06:58.050 --> 00:07:01.300
Well, you were fatigued
by the time you got here...

00:07:01.300 --> 00:07:03.950
...and, more importantly, your 
attention was drawn to the Captain.

00:07:04.950 --> 00:07:07.140
I barely caught the 
moment of your inattention.

00:07:07.140 --> 00:07:09.800
If we'd fought on the equal footing, 
I probably wouldn't have stood a chance.

00:07:09.800 --> 00:07:10.950
Well...

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:12.690
Thanks to you,
I got some good exercise.

00:07:18.940 --> 00:07:20.140
The battle exercise is finished.

00:07:20.140 --> 00:07:22.090
Injured, report to the medical room.

00:07:22.090 --> 00:07:24.160
Check for damage
to inboard facilities.

00:07:25.890 --> 00:07:28.430
LTJG Kircheis is so strong.

00:07:28.430 --> 00:07:31.850
Indeed, the Security 
Chief is no slouch.

00:07:31.850 --> 00:07:33.400
He's not just another kid.

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:37.750
In December of Imperial Year 483...

00:07:37.750 --> 00:07:46.000
...after eliminating an enemy cruiser with his 
destroyer in the 5th Battle of Iserlohn Fortress...

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:51.870
...Reinhard was promoted to Commander and was assigned to captain the cruiser, Hershrichlenchen.

00:07:55.150 --> 00:07:57.950
But to Reinhard's dissatisfaction...

00:07:57.950 --> 00:08:02.170
...he couldn't manage to assign Kircheis as his first officer and he remained a LTJG.

00:08:03.560 --> 00:08:07.950
In the end, he had no choice but to accept the personnel decision of the brass...

00:08:07.950 --> 00:08:11.750
...Lt. Commander Wahlen stayed on in the
position he had already occupied as First Officer...

00:08:11.750 --> 00:08:13.860
...and Kircheis became the security chief.

00:08:14.830 --> 00:08:19.460
Since security chiefs are also the personal guards for the captain, they are always at the captain's side.

00:08:19.460 --> 00:08:20.850
He decided to be content with that.

00:08:22.050 --> 00:08:23.950
It had been several months
since this appointment...

00:08:23.950 --> 00:08:25.950
...and since there were no large-scale attacks by the Alliance Forces...

00:08:25.950 --> 00:08:30.650
...time passed without any opportunity for the battlefield accolades that Reinhard hoped for.

00:08:32.920 --> 00:08:38.150
Commander Musel, how long has it been since you were appointed as captain of a cruiser ?

00:08:39.710 --> 00:08:41.650
It'll be half a year soon.

00:08:42.820 --> 00:08:47.510
During that time, there has been no opportunity
for battle but it seems you've been preparing well.

00:08:47.510 --> 00:08:50.350
From what I've heard, you've been
rigorously training your subordinates.

00:08:51.100 --> 00:08:52.350
I feel embarrassed.

00:08:52.350 --> 00:08:53.850
No, it's a good thing.

00:08:58.090 --> 00:09:00.820
I called you in for a reason.

00:09:00.820 --> 00:09:03.900
I've heard good things about you, and 
there's a mission I'd like you to undertake.

00:09:05.150 --> 00:09:06.880
What kind of a mission might it be ?

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:13.950
If you'd like to know, I must
have you sign this oath first.

00:09:13.950 --> 00:09:15.550
This is a top secret mission.

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:21.280
You have the right to decline the mission
after you're informed of its requirements...

00:09:21.280 --> 00:09:26.050
...but even in that case, the contents of the mission must remain confidential.

00:09:30.670 --> 00:09:31.870
I understand.

00:09:41.880 --> 00:09:43.010
He's signed it.

00:09:43.010 --> 00:09:43.690
Please come in.

00:09:53.650 --> 00:09:57.710
This is Rear Admiral Arbentraut from the 
3rd Strategic Division of High Command HQ.

00:09:57.710 --> 00:09:59.690
The Rear Admiral will provide you with an explanation{of the mission}.

00:10:10.660 --> 00:10:13.650
So you're Commander Musel.

00:10:13.650 --> 00:10:15.240
I've heard a lot about you.

00:10:17.230 --> 00:10:18.250
I'm flattered.

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:24.950
Getting to the subject, do you
know who Count Helksheimer is ?

00:10:26.700 --> 00:10:30.100
He was told that Count Helksheimer had fallen from favor...

00:10:30.100 --> 00:10:33.560
...and had escaped to the Phezzani 
Autonomous Territory with all of his family.

00:10:33.560 --> 00:10:36.460
Moreover, he was smuggling out an important military secret...

00:10:36.460 --> 00:10:40.100
...and was planning to defect to the 
Alliance with the secret as a souvenir.

00:10:40.100 --> 00:10:41.750
The military wanted
to prevent it somehow...

00:10:41.750 --> 00:10:45.540
...but they could not send a battleship past the Phezzani Corridor.

00:10:45.540 --> 00:10:48.050
Therefore, the cruiser
Hershrichlenchen...

00:10:48.050 --> 00:10:52.090
...must independently enter Alliance 
territory through the Iserlohn Corridor...

00:10:52.090 --> 00:10:54.090
...and make our way
to the Phezzan Corridor...

00:10:54.090 --> 00:10:58.500
...to the exit on the Alliance side,
and either capture or destroy it{i.e. Helksheimer's ship}.

00:11:00.500 --> 00:11:03.350
It's an independent mission
within enemy territory...{to himself}

00:11:03.850 --> 00:11:08.300
Moreover, since it's a secret mission, I cannot expect open support.

00:11:08.300 --> 00:11:10.350
This is not an easy mission.

00:11:11.040 --> 00:11:13.220
But still...

00:11:19.660 --> 00:11:21.550
May I ask a question ?

00:11:23.720 --> 00:11:25.160
What is it ?

00:11:25.160 --> 00:11:29.590
Is it not possible to order the Phezzani government to prevent his defection ?

00:11:29.590 --> 00:11:30.950
Even though it's an 
autonomous territory...

00:11:30.950 --> 00:11:34.310
...they must still have an obligation to be loyal to the Empire, I presume ?

00:11:36.180 --> 00:11:39.950
Last year, the 5th head of the
autonomous territory was just appointed...

00:11:39.950 --> 00:11:42.600
...a man named Adrian Rubinsky...

00:11:42.600 --> 00:11:45.240
...and he's very difficult to deal with.

00:11:45.240 --> 00:11:46.950
If we pressure him or
take forceful measures...

00:11:46.950 --> 00:11:53.350
...he might invite the rebels into the Phezzan Corridor and put up resistance against the Empire.

00:11:53.750 --> 00:11:56.600
I see, he's that kind of a man.

00:11:56.600 --> 00:11:58.810
Is this a sign of change in the era ?

00:11:59.970 --> 00:12:04.350
Still, they're making
Helksheimer stay there for a while.

00:12:04.350 --> 00:12:06.550
Right now, that's as
cooperative as they're getting.

00:12:07.450 --> 00:12:10.250
How about the Imperial Military Liaison Officer at the commissioner's office ?

00:12:10.250 --> 00:12:14.600
Despite the title, the Imperial Military Liaison Officer has no forces at his command.

00:12:14.600 --> 00:12:17.290
Intelligence gathering is about
as much as he can do.

00:12:17.290 --> 00:12:20.540
Plus, Helksheimer has
his own private troops.

00:12:20.540 --> 00:12:22.920
It's impossible to
prevent it{i.e. Helksheimer's defection} with force.

00:12:23.740 --> 00:12:24.500
I see.

00:12:29.130 --> 00:12:33.080
But it's not like they're idling.

00:12:33.080 --> 00:12:35.050
They won't be stingy with
cooperation on intelligence.

00:12:35.950 --> 00:12:37.160
I wonder.

00:12:37.160 --> 00:12:38.970
I don't think I can 
expect much from them.

00:12:40.520 --> 00:12:42.350
I'd like to ask one more question.

00:12:42.350 --> 00:12:45.200
What is the "military
secret" in question ?

00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:47.150
Without knowing what it is, I wonder if it'll be possible for me to retrieve it.

00:12:50.150 --> 00:12:51.350
You're right.

00:12:53.400 --> 00:12:59.600
What I'd like to have you retrieve is the test unit for the directional Seffle Particle generator.

00:13:00.280 --> 00:13:03.070
Directional Seffle Particles ?

00:13:03.070 --> 00:13:06.050
I've read about the
possibility in a dissertation...

00:13:06.050 --> 00:13:08.500
...but I wasn't aware that its
invention had been successful.

00:13:10.450 --> 00:13:14.100
Of course, it's an
important military secret.

00:13:14.100 --> 00:13:16.810
But even though it's still
in the experimental stage...

00:13:16.810 --> 00:13:20.950
...the Science and Engineering Department has put maximum effort into its development...

00:13:20.950 --> 00:13:24.790
...on the proposal from Inspector General Shaft who's recently been appointed to the position.

00:13:24.790 --> 00:13:26.700
It's only a matter of time
before it becomes operational.

00:13:27.700 --> 00:13:33.990
But if this secret is leaked to the rebels, our advantage will be lost.

00:13:33.990 --> 00:13:36.480
That's how important this mission is.

00:13:37.460 --> 00:13:39.210
I see.

00:13:40.520 --> 00:13:46.360
But at this point, I can't quite say I have a
firm command over the loyalty of my crew.

00:13:46.360 --> 00:13:48.700
The difficulties are beyond imagination.

00:13:53.930 --> 00:13:57.210
But still, this is an
incredible opportunity.

00:14:10.120 --> 00:14:11.330
I understand.

00:14:11.330 --> 00:14:12.400
I accept this mission.

00:14:13.110 --> 00:14:16.040
I hate to dampen your enthusiasm, but since this is a secret mission...

00:14:16.040 --> 00:14:18.600
...it will not appear in your
official file or military records.

00:14:18.600 --> 00:14:20.740
A certificate of war participation will not be issued, either.

00:14:20.740 --> 00:14:23.760
But it will count toward
personnel evaluation.

00:14:23.760 --> 00:14:25.230
Despite this, do you still accept ?

00:14:25.230 --> 00:14:26.350
I'm aware of it.

00:14:29.730 --> 00:14:31.000
Very well, then.

00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:34.820
My subordinate, Lt. Commander Bendling, is waiting outside.

00:14:34.820 --> 00:14:40.000
He will assist you with details of
information and miscellaneous preparations.

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:42.700
He'll accompany you on the mission.

00:14:42.700 --> 00:14:44.570
A watchdog, huh ?

00:14:46.550 --> 00:14:50.050
Then, if you'll excuse me, I'd like
to begin preparations immediately.

00:14:50.050 --> 00:14:52.300
It appears there's not
much time to waste.

00:15:05.240 --> 00:15:08.380
But really, I wonder if this will turn out well, with such a stripling at the helm.

00:15:08.380 --> 00:15:11.040
That's an unexpected
statement from you.

00:15:11.040 --> 00:15:13.800
I thought you were the one who appointed Commander Musel.

00:15:14.380 --> 00:15:16.890
I only received the order.

00:15:16.890 --> 00:15:18.750
Oh, don't ask me where
the order came from.

00:15:26.780 --> 00:15:28.020
You must be Captain Musel.

00:15:28.750 --> 00:15:32.450
I'm Lt. Commander von Bendling,
from High Command Headquarters.

00:15:32.450 --> 00:15:36.550
I will be accompanying you
on this mission as an inspector.

00:15:36.550 --> 00:15:37.550
An inspector ?

00:15:38.970 --> 00:15:41.890
Um...no, "Inspector" is just a title.

00:15:41.890 --> 00:15:45.140
It's more like an advisor, or assistant...

00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:48.450
You mean a watchdog.

00:15:48.450 --> 00:15:49.550
Well, thanks for taking the trouble.

00:15:51.710 --> 00:15:54.390
What I want from you is one thing...

00:15:54.390 --> 00:15:58.820
...to provide me with all the information up to this point accurately and without omissions.

00:15:58.820 --> 00:16:00.360
That's all.

00:16:00.360 --> 00:16:02.750
No further advice or 
assistance is necessary.

00:16:02.750 --> 00:16:07.250
Furthermore, there's no need for you to butt in on the operational plans we'll employ.

00:16:07.250 --> 00:16:09.850
If you can't accept that, I won't permit you to accompany us.

00:16:09.850 --> 00:16:12.880
I'll have you wait inside the fortress for the good news, so what do you plan to do ?

00:16:12.880 --> 00:16:14.950
I...I understand.

00:16:15.890 --> 00:16:17.260
Good.

00:16:17.260 --> 00:16:18.190
Then come with me.

00:16:27.170 --> 00:16:34.010
On the next day, cruiser Hershrichlenchen, pretending to be on a training voyage swiftly departed Iserlohn.

00:16:34.780 --> 00:16:40.350
At this point, Reinhard had
disclosed the mission only to Kircheis.

00:16:48.510 --> 00:16:53.650
It was not until his ship came close to
the Alliance side of the Iserlohn Corridor...

00:16:53.650 --> 00:16:57.100
...that Reinhard revealed the true objective of their voyage.

00:16:58.680 --> 00:17:01.250
As long as those are our
orders, I have no objection...

00:17:01.250 --> 00:17:04.160
...but isn't this an 
excessively reckless mission ?

00:17:04.160 --> 00:17:06.940
Your concern is warranted, No. 1.

00:17:06.940 --> 00:17:12.200
To encroach upon enemy territory with a lone cruiser is, as you say, reckless.

00:17:12.200 --> 00:17:14.000
I think everyone will agree.

00:17:14.790 --> 00:17:18.940
But because of that, the enemy
will not expect such a situation.

00:17:18.940 --> 00:17:20.700
That gives us a chance.

00:17:24.730 --> 00:17:27.700
But first, there's the enemy patrol line at the exit of the Iserlohn Corridor;

00:17:27.700 --> 00:17:30.740
Penetrating through that
will be difficult enough.

00:17:30.740 --> 00:17:33.380
What do you plan to do, Captain ?

00:17:34.080 --> 00:17:37.560
The corridor exit is a large expanse.

00:17:37.560 --> 00:17:40.200
It's not like there's no space for even an ant to squirm through.

00:17:41.150 --> 00:17:45.170
There's plenty of space for a single cruiser to slide past.

00:17:52.150 --> 00:17:54.210
If there isn't such a place,
we can just create one.

00:18:00.510 --> 00:18:05.560
It wasn't that the crew was satisfied with the plan,
but if those were their orders they must obey them.

00:18:05.560 --> 00:18:08.920
Reinhard didn't bother to provide a detailed explanation either.

00:18:08.920 --> 00:18:13.530
For he knew, that in order to gain their loyalty, he had to demonstrate his capabilities.

00:18:14.990 --> 00:18:16.250
Closing in on the
enemy patrol line !

00:18:17.410 --> 00:18:19.700
All crew, prepare for battle.

00:18:19.700 --> 00:18:20.900
Maintain course as is.

00:18:22.770 --> 00:18:26.100
Captain, are you planning a forced entry ?

00:18:26.100 --> 00:18:28.090
No. 1, execute my order.

00:18:33.360 --> 00:18:35.310
All crew, prepare for battle.

00:18:35.310 --> 00:18:36.100
Maintain course.

00:18:40.040 --> 00:18:41.390
Entering enemy patrol zone !

00:18:42.860 --> 00:18:44.800
Increase the output of the beacons.

00:18:44.800 --> 00:18:47.700
And set the radar at all
ranges to maximum.

00:18:47.990 --> 00:18:49.170
Captain !

00:18:49.170 --> 00:18:53.100
That's like telling the 
enemy to come find us !

00:18:53.100 --> 00:18:54.360
Precisely.

00:18:54.360 --> 00:18:55.680
Why don't we have them find us ?

00:19:07.400 --> 00:19:08.590
Enemy ships are approaching !

00:19:09.260 --> 00:19:10.210
Monitor !

00:19:10.210 --> 00:19:11.060
How many ?

00:19:11.060 --> 00:19:14.330
Three cruisers,
and about 15 destroyers.

00:19:14.330 --> 00:19:16.540
They're presumed to
be the patrol unit !

00:19:16.540 --> 00:19:17.920
Captain.

00:19:18.740 --> 00:19:19.990
This is good.

00:19:19.990 --> 00:19:24.430
Maintain course, and then just before we enter their effective range, fire the main cannon.

00:19:24.430 --> 00:19:28.100
Then turn around and withdraw in the 4 o'clock direction.

00:19:28.100 --> 00:19:29.200
Captain.

00:19:29.200 --> 00:19:30.560
No. 1.

00:19:31.270 --> 00:19:33.270
Main cannon, prepare to fire.

00:19:33.270 --> 00:19:36.780
Reconnaissance personnel, ten second countdown before we enter the enemy's effective range.

00:19:36.780 --> 00:19:41.200
Chief Navigator, calculate a new route in the 4 o'clock direction.

00:19:41.200 --> 00:19:45.410
Engine room, be prepared for 
maximum battle speed at any time.

00:19:46.260 --> 00:19:47.700
Enemy effective range in -

00:19:47.700 --> 00:19:49.150
...ten...

00:19:49.150 --> 00:19:50.600
...nine...

00:19:50.600 --> 00:19:51.950
...eight...

00:19:51.950 --> 00:19:53.350
...seven...

00:19:52.840 --> 00:19:54.910
Upon my signal, fire the cannon.

00:19:53.350 --> 00:19:54.800
...six...

00:19:54.800 --> 00:19:56.000
...five...

00:19:54.910 --> 00:19:56.730
After firing, turn the
ship around immediately.

00:19:56.000 --> 00:19:57.350
...four...

00:19:57.350 --> 00:19:57.740
...three...

00:19:57.740 --> 00:19:58.300
Fire !

00:20:05.300 --> 00:20:06.600
Impact confirmed.

00:20:06.600 --> 00:20:08.590
It seems to have been
repelled by their shield.

00:20:08.590 --> 00:20:09.300
The enemy ships are pursuing us !

00:20:10.380 --> 00:20:11.600
That's all good.

00:20:13.900 --> 00:20:15.050
Enemy ships are firing.

00:20:15.050 --> 00:20:15.700
Shots are coming !

00:20:20.500 --> 00:20:21.800
Don't be flustered.

00:20:21.800 --> 00:20:23.580
We're out of their effective range.

00:20:23.580 --> 00:20:28.990
Maintaining this distance, we'll
draw them into our patrol fleet !

00:20:38.680 --> 00:20:40.900
LTJG Kircheis was aware of this ?

00:20:43.450 --> 00:20:48.820
Accompanied by the enemy fleet,
Hershrichlenchen returned to the Corridor...

00:20:48.820 --> 00:20:51.770
...and deliberately caused them to 
encounter their friendly patrol fleet.

00:20:52.780 --> 00:20:55.190
There's our patrol fleet ahead of us.

00:20:55.190 --> 00:20:55.880
Good.

00:20:55.880 --> 00:20:57.170
We'll make them bump into one another.

00:21:09.420 --> 00:21:11.040
Make a turn again in
the 4 o'clock direction !

00:21:35.660 --> 00:21:38.300
Using the enemy's frequency,
send a rescue signal.

00:21:38.300 --> 00:21:39.430
At maximum output.

00:21:40.500 --> 00:21:43.400
Are you attracting the enemy
patrol units into this space area ?

00:21:46.100 --> 00:21:47.680
That's right.

00:21:47.680 --> 00:21:50.850
Afterwards, we'll penetrate through the
area where the enemy lines are thinnest.

00:21:53.710 --> 00:21:57.150
Captain, we can shut off the
beacons and radar now, can't we ?

00:21:57.150 --> 00:21:59.000
Yeah, you're right.

00:21:59.000 --> 00:22:02.350
Shut them off, and switch 
monitoring to passive sensors only.

00:22:02.350 --> 00:22:03.760
Shutting down beacons and radar.

00:22:05.250 --> 00:22:10.150
Captain, you're using our friendly patrol fleet almost like a decoy.

00:22:10.150 --> 00:22:11.530
Isn't that...

00:22:12.250 --> 00:22:17.900
Even though we're undertaking a difficult mission, they say these are secret orders...

00:22:17.900 --> 00:22:21.050
...and can't give us any assistance, so I just thought I'd force them to help us.

00:22:21.050 --> 00:22:25.970
Besides, for the outermost front-line patrol units skirmishes are an every day occurrence.

00:22:25.970 --> 00:22:28.950
I just orchestrated this
to take advantage of it.

00:22:33.170 --> 00:22:36.680
Even though our captain is young, he's no an ordinary man.

00:22:38.460 --> 00:22:40.150
Just as Reinhard planned...

00:22:40.150 --> 00:22:43.810
...the Alliance patrol units gathered
their friendly units, and in response...

00:22:43.810 --> 00:22:50.970
...the Imperials also called in for patrol reinforcements, so the battle gradually became larger and larger.

00:22:50.970 --> 00:22:52.150
At the same time...

00:22:52.150 --> 00:22:55.850
...the patrols in the other space-areas of the corridor exit became thinner.

00:22:55.850 --> 00:23:00.510
The cruiser Hershrichlenchen succeeded in encroaching upon Alliance territory.

